% A minus and the digits after it are one negative literal wherever a term
% stands, with or without space between them: the two facts below are one
% fact, and the least 64-bit integer can be written although its magnitude
% alone is out of range.
offset(start, -1).
offset(start, - 1).
least(-9223372036854775808).
shifted(X, -2) :- offset(X, - 1).

offset(start, X)?
least(X)?
shifted(start, Y), Y < -1?
